# Bands of procedural skin, one per line, sorted coarse to fine when loaded:
# name, primitive, wavelength in millimetres, amplitude, field, seed, and for points and curves
# density, profile, width in millimetres, the band it depends on (- for none) and stretch.
# Height is in millimetres; melanin and hemoglobin deviate from the material's base values. A dip
# profile subtracts, so a negative amplitude raises: freckles darken.
#
# Weights compare a band's scale with texels and pixels: the wavelength of noise, the width of
# points and curves. Scales here step by about 2.5, so a lookup two levels coarser than wanted
# leaves at most about three bands to add live.
tone_broad     noise   40      0.12      melanin     11
tone_mid       noise   15      0.08      hemoglobin  12
tone_fine      noise   6       0.05      melanin     13
freckles       points  9       -0.25     melanin     41   0.15  dip      2.5     -        1
relief_broad   noise   1.0     0.03      height      21
wrinkles       curves  5       0.05      height      51   0.35  line     0.4     -        1
creases        curves  1.5     0.012     height      52   0.4   line     0.16    -        1
furrows        points  0.35    0.04      height      42   1     network  0.06    -        1.6
pores          points  0.35    0.025     height      43   0.7   dip      0.025   furrows  1
lines          points  0.08    0.006     height      44   1     network  0.01    -        1.3
plates         points  0.035   0.0012    height      45   1     plate    0.004   -        1
grain_1        noise   0.0016  0.00007   height      31
grain_2        noise   0.00065 0.000028  height      32
grain_3        noise   0.00026 0.000011  height      33
